1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,552
Almost every fast food sign is red and yellow.

2
00:00:02,752 --> 00:00:03,797
That's not an accident.

3
00:00:04,197 --> 00:00:06,608
Watch. Max is walking home. Not hungry. At all.

4
00:00:06,808 --> 00:00:10,627
Gray street. Gray buildings. Then, bam! A giant red and yellow sign.

5
00:00:10,827 --> 00:00:13,152
Red grabs your eye faster than almost any color.

6
00:00:13,352 --> 00:00:16,253
Yellow is one of the easiest colors to spot from far away.

7
00:00:16,453 --> 00:00:18,395
Together, they scream: stop here. Right now.

8
00:00:18,595 --> 00:00:20,856
And red is often linked with energy and appetite.

9
00:00:21,056 --> 00:00:22,421
Suddenly, Max is starving.

10
00:00:22,621 --> 00:00:23,603
His feet just turn.

11
00:00:24,003 --> 00:00:26,520
Inside? Bright lights, bright colors, upbeat music.

12
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:28,213
The whole room says: hurry up.

13
00:00:28,413 --> 00:00:31,507
Some studies found faster music can make people eat faster.

14
00:00:31,707 --> 00:00:34,181
Chomp, chomp, chomp. Burger gone in ninety seconds.

15
00:00:34,381 --> 00:00:35,747
And the seats? Hard plastic.

16
00:00:35,947 --> 00:00:38,144
Comfy enough to eat. Not comfy enough to stay.

17
00:00:38,344 --> 00:00:41,459
Because a table that empties fast is ready for the next customer.

18
00:00:41,659 --> 00:00:44,325
Next customer. Next tray. Next order. All day long.

19
00:00:44,725 --> 00:00:48,117
Max walked in for nothing. He walked out with a combo and a milkshake.

20
00:00:48,317 --> 00:00:49,811
It's not magic. It's design.

21
00:00:50,011 --> 00:00:53,467
So next time a red and yellow sign makes you hungry, ask yourself:

22
00:00:53,667 --> 00:00:55,032
Am I hungry? Or is the sign?

